{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ואך את הדבר", :translit "v'ach et ha-davar", :gloss "but only the matter"} {:he "אך חלק", :translit "ach cheilek", :gloss "but only a portion"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: the word אך in Numbers 22:20 is interpreted via Proverbs 13:23 where אך means a separating/dividing limitation."}], :frame {:text "The particle אך ('only/but') functions throughout Tanakh as a word of limitation and restriction, as seen in passages such as Genesis 17:22 and Genesis 41:16. The Ba'al HaTurim reads the word אך in Numbers 22:20 in light of the phrase אך חלק in Proverbs 13:23, which he understands as denoting a separation or division, to show that God's permission to Balaam was strictly partitioned.", :sources ["Proverbs 13:23" "Genesis 17:22" "Genesis 41:16"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: the word אך in Numbers 22:20 is interpreted via Proverbs 13:23 where אך means a separating/dividing limitation.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:30:42.689610591Z", :model "glm-5.2"}